 a  bunch of stuff back in you you are you  are getting rid of the superfluous  things now is there someone you know out  in the country like I live in Montana  and in Missoula and like you know this  is one of the big cities like 68,000  people here but there are there are  certainly there are certainly cities  outside of here with you know 100 or 200  people in there and yeah like a farmer's  gonna have to hold on to some extra  bolts and maybe they've got you know a  tractor that they use for spare parts  and they're actually using that again  we're not propagating people just throw  out everything what we're saying is is  that you know look look at your  surroundings if it is stressing you out  there there is a way out if there's  clutter around you there is a way out  and not just that but the the decisions  we make every day to bring in things  into our lives whether it's physical  possessions or whether it is a  relationship whatever it may be  to do that more deliberately instead of  oh well you know I've got this actually  I got this bonus check and I could put a  down payment on this new car that looked  really cool with the bow wrapped around  it in the in the driveway for you know  that that husband got that wife is a  gift I'm gonna do that for my wife and  then going into debt I mean those are  that's a bad example of what to do with  our resources yeah um but I'd like to  think that minimalism helps people kind  of find that balance of especially you  know for poor people who have to be even  more deliberate with their resources to  help them kind of decide what is going  to add value one isn't going to add  value but yeah man certainly everyone  different circumstances everyone has  different you know socioeconomic  backgrounds and in current situations  but you know living deliberately living  intentionally I would you know I would  hate to discriminate against poor people  and say that that they aren't able to  live or they aren't able to see benefits  from living intentionally or living  deliberately I would I'd say that they  have just as much of an ability to have  positive effects from that than someone  who's rich  the documentary again is the minimalist  we've been speaking with one of the film  subjects Ryan Nicodemus super  interesting thanks so much for talking  to me today and will absolutely continue  to recommend the documentary to people  awesome and thanks for having me on the  show
 

